## Objective
- Perform adversarial review of phase `phase-097` ("Parse and format dates from text") and report wrong or unproven behaviour in the exact `FINDINGS:` / `REVIEW VERDICT:` format required by the RBOPS reviewer contract.
- The review is read-only; findings must cite `file:line` actually read, and every BLOCKER needs a `VERIFIED:` marker.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`.
- Available tools: `glob`, `grep`, `read`; `bash` is unavailable. Cannot run tests or inspect external Cargo registry paths.
- Contract: hostile review, hunt fake completion, panic/UB, resource limits, nondeterminism, error regressions, spec drift, missing edge tests, scope.
- A BLOCKER without `VERIFIED:` must be reported as MAJOR. If unsure, report MAJOR and state what would settle it.
- Final output must end with exactly `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`, and nothing after it.
- Phase changes add `time.parse`, date-aware `time.format`/`time.unix`, `nanosecond` date property, plus SPEC/README/SURVEY/test updates.
- Change set includes: `README.md`, `SPEC.md`, `SURVEY.md`, `phases/phase-097/REPORT.md`, `src/runtime.rs`, `src/stdlib.rs`, `tests/doc_blocks_runs.txt`, `tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs`, `tests/time_builtin_test.rs`.

