FINDINGS:

1. **[MAJOR]** `src/runtime.rs:909-916` — `time.format` still panics on a layout chrono accepts but cannot format. `formatted_date` rejects only `Item::Error` at line 910, then calls `date.format(format).to_string()` at line 916. Chrono’s `%#z` is a parse-only `Fixed::Internal` item, not `Item::Error`, so `time.format(time.date(2024, 1, 1), "%#z")` reaches a `fmt::Error` and `to_string` panics. This contradicts `phases/phase-097/REPORT.md:35-36` and `SPEC.md:1538-1539`; the only refusal test uses `%Q` (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:837`). Fix by formatting into a `String` with `write!` and mapping `fmt::Error` to a catchable `Runtime` error, and add a `%#z` test. Not run here; a one-line probe would settle it.

2. **[MAJOR]** `src/runtime.rs:648-671` and `src/value.rs:353` — the positive window boundary does not round-trip. `date_year` accepts an optional `-` but not `+`; `time.parse("10000-01-01")` is accepted and `unix_seconds_for` accepts `253402300800` (`src/runtime.rs:926-927`), but `%Y` formats that date as `+10000-01-01 ...`, which `date_year` rejects at position 0. Thus `time.unix(to_text(time.parse("10000-01-01")))` fails, and `time.format(253402300800)` produces text that `time.unix`/`time.parse` cannot read. The boundary test stops at 9999 and calls it “the last year a date can name” (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:330-334`), hiding the mismatch. The comment at `src/runtime.rs:644-646` also claims old `time.unix` read `10000-01-01`, but `phases/phase-035/FINDINGS.md:81-83` says chrono rejected years above 9999 at parse. Fix by accepting `+` in `date_year` and documenting it, or lowering `MAX_SECONDS`; add a positive-boundary round-trip test.

3. **[MAJOR]** `src/runtime.rs:711-719`, `756-776`, `861-869` — the new range checks have no test. The malformed-input list (`tests/time_builtin_test.rs:859-869`) never passes month 13, hour 24, minute 60, day 0/32, or offset minute 60 to `time.parse`; the only month-13 test is the constructor at `tests/time_builtin_test.rs:504`. `phases/phase-097/REPORT.md:55` nevertheless claims “month 13” under the parse `out_of_bounds` row. Under the contract, a new branch with no test is a MAJOR. Add parse tests for `"2024-13-01"`, `"2024-00-01"`, `"2024-01-32"`, `"2024-01-01T24:00:00"`, `"2024-01-01T00:60:00"`, and `"2024-01-01T00:00:00+02:60"`, asserting the reported position and catchability.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 3
